  "answer_text": "In *The Vampire Diaries*, Elena's transformation into a vampire is a major turning point in the series. Here's a full breakdown:\n\n### When Does Elena Turn?\n\nElena Gilbert begins her transition into a vampire during the **Season 3 finale**, titled **\"The Departed\"** (Episode 22), when she drowns after being in a car accident with Matt Donovan.\n\nThough Dr. Meredith Fell had secretly given Elena vampire blood to heal an earlier injury, this leads to her transformation when she dies.\n\nShe **officially transitions** into a vampire in the **first episode of Season 4**, titled **\"Growing Pains.\"**\n\n---\n\n### How Did It Happen?\n\nRebekah deliberately caused the vehicle carrying Elena and Matt to crash off Wickery Bridge and plunge into the water. Although a distraught Stefan arrived on time to save them, Elena urged him to save Matt first \u2014 and by the time Stefan pulled Elena out of the water, she had breathed her last.\n\nUnbeknownst to everyone involved, Elena had vampire blood in her system when she died, as Dr. Meredith Fell had injected it into her to save her from fatal injuries inflicted by Klaus.\n\n---\n\n### Completing the Transition\n\nHer full transformation occurs in **Season 4, Episode 1** (\"Growing Pains\"), where she wakes up in transition and must make the difficult decision to complete the process by drinking human blood.\n\nShe became a vampire **despite never wanting to be one.**\n\n---\n\n### Does She Remain a Vampire?\n\nElena woke up as a vampire in Season 3, Episode 22 and remained a vampire for all of **Seasons 4, 5, and 6**, only getting cured back into a human at the **end of Season 6**.",
